win32u: answer the adapter info queries we can, instead of failing all of them

NtGdiDdDDIQueryAdapterInfo returns STATUS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED for every type in this
tree's 10.0 base. Upstream has since answered two of them, in c06f38f4a5 and
6e0eab205e (both 2025-02-11), later bumped by 8b62bd3243 "win32u: Bump D3DKMT
driver version." (2026-05-06). Those two cases, the QAI_DRIVERVERSION enum and
the WDDM 3.1 value are that work backported verbatim, so a future rebase onto
11.x drops the hunk cleanly. Upstream's own test now expects >= WDDM 3.1.

KMTQAITYPE_WDDM_2_7_CAPS is not upstream, it comes from Proton (proton_11.0,
dlls/win32u/d3dkmt.c), and this is the part that is deliberately not a verbatim
port. Proton fetches VkPhysicalDeviceDriverPropertiesKHR for the adapter and
sets HwSchSupported / HwSchEnabled / HwSchEnabledByDefault only when driverID is
VK_DRIVER_ID_NVIDIA_PROPRIETARY, because hardware scheduling there means NVIDIA
doing userspace submission; every other driver, and the WINE_DISABLE_HARDWARE_
SCHEDULING escape hatch, leaves all four bits clear.

On Apple silicon that condition cannot be true. There is no NVIDIA proprietary
driver to match, so Proton's algorithm evaluates to a zeroed caps block for every
adapter, every time, and the Vulkan round trip it takes to get there is pure
cost. Answering with the zeroed block directly is the same result computed for
nothing, and it needs no adapter lookup, since with the driverID check gone
there is nothing left to read off the adapter. All four bits are true of this
stack independently anyway: D3DMetal does not expose GPU-side scheduling and
winemac.drv has no independent VidPn VSync control.

diff --git i/dlls/win32u/d3dkmt.c w/dlls/win32u/d3dkmt.c
index 24a668a8..a7f7a647 100644
--- i/dlls/win32u/d3dkmt.c
+++ w/dlls/win32u/d3dkmt.c
@@ -333,10 +333,49 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtGdiDdDDIDestroyDevice( const D3DKMT_DESTROYDEVICE *desc )
  */
 NTSTATUS WINAPI NtGdiDdDDIQueryAdapterInfo( D3DKMT_QUERYADAPTERINFO *desc )
 {
-    if (!desc) return STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER;
+    TRACE( "(%p).\n", desc );
 
-    FIXME( "desc %p, type %d stub\n", desc, desc->Type );
-    return STATUS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED;
+    if (!desc || !desc->hAdapter || !desc->pPrivateDriverData)
+        return STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER;
+
+    switch (desc->Type)
+    {
+    case KMTQAITYPE_CHECKDRIVERUPDATESTATUS:
+    {
+        BOOL *value = desc->pPrivateDriverData;
+
+        if (desc->PrivateDriverDataSize < sizeof(*value))
+            return STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER;
+
+        *value = FALSE;
+        return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+    }
+    case KMTQAITYPE_DRIVERVERSION:
+    {
+        D3DKMT_DRIVERVERSION *value = desc->pPrivateDriverData;
+
+        if (desc->PrivateDriverDataSize < sizeof(*value))
+            return STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER;
+
+        *value = KMT_DRIVERVERSION_WDDM_3_1;
+        return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+    }
+    case KMTQAITYPE_WDDM_2_7_CAPS:
+    {
+        D3DKMT_WDDM_2_7_CAPS *value = desc->pPrivateDriverData;
+
+        if (desc->PrivateDriverDataSize < sizeof(*value))
+            return STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER;
+
+        memset( value, 0, sizeof(*value) );
+        return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+    }
+    default:
+    {
+        FIXME( "type %d not handled.\n", desc->Type );
+        return STATUS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED;
+    }
+    }
 }
 
 /******************************************************************************
